solution:
In right triangle $VWX$ with the right angle at $W$, $VX = \sqrt{13}$ and $VW = 3$. Using the Pythagorean theorem, $WX = \sqrt{VX^2 - VW^2} = \sqrt{13 - 9} = 2$. The tangent of angle $V$ is the ratio of the opposite side to the adjacent side:
$$ \tan V = \frac{WX}{VW} = \frac{2}{3} $$
\boxed{\frac{2}{3}}

